\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar edges up on BOJ easing hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 06:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO Sept 21 (Reuters) - The dollar edged higher against the yen by midday in Tokyo, supported by speculation the Bank of Japan (BOJ) may ease monetary policy to get the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But the market remained largely directionless until the results of the BOJ's Policy Board meeting later this afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Buying by Japanese investors and short-covering by overseas speculators pushed the dollar to a high near 107.38 yen. But the greenback pared gains on profit-taking and selling, possibly from Japanese accounts. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 106.80/90 yen, up from 106.25/35 yen in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We're pretty much smack in the middle of the range between Monday's highs slightly above 108 and overnight lows just below 106, so the market is basically on hold until the BOJ policy board meeting ends, a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues are likely to be discussed at this week's meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors from Group of Seven (G7) industrial nations, although a formal agenda has not been set. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had briefly fallen to a low of 105.87 yen overnight, according to dealers, on speculation that Japan had failed to get the United States to agree to take joint action to stem the yen's rise, based on a U.S. consulting firm report. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said that although it had not been decided if \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be included in the key agenda for Saturday's G-7 meeting, the subject is likely to be discussed given the recent market situation. \par \par \uc2  He also said the yen's rise was likely to be discussed at the BOJ's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  There is a growing consensus that the BOJ will have to at least make a gesture indicating it will provide more liquidity in the money market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "It's difficult to say what the reaction will be, as it will depend on the extent that the BOJ is willing to ease," a city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  If the BOJ adopts some form of quantitative easing, the dollar may be lifted above 108 yen to near 110 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  If the BOJ's decision to ease is limited, the dollar will likely be sold, but the greenback's decline may be stemmed near 105 yen, they also said. \par \par \uc2  Yet if the BOJ keeps policy unchanged and makes no reference to possible further easing, the dollar may test 103.20 yen, the lowest level since December 1995, or further towards 100 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Even if the BOJ's decision in itself is a disappointment, there are still some risks ahead of the G7 meeting, so selling may be limited," the city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's upward move would be rather sluggish, while a move to the downside would be quick" as the underlying yen-buying trend will likely remain intact, another city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are also awaiting the results at 0530 GMT of a 10-year Japanese government bond auction. The Finance Ministry offered 1.4 trillion yen worth of 10-year JGBs with a coupon of 1.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was firm against the dollar on speculation of strong business sentiment figures for Germany. \par \par \uc2  The closely-watched Ifo business climate index will be released at 0800 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast, on average, the headline west German business climate index rose to 94.4 in August, up from 93.6 in July and the highest level in a year. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at $1.0375/80, up from $1.0354/59 in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at 110.82/95 yen, up from 110.09 yen in New York late on Monday. ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9l00b0y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
