\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Eyeing Further Easing, Newspaper Says - Kyodo \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 1999\par 02:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept. 18 (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan is considering measures to further ease its monetary grip ahead of Tuesday's meeting of its policy-setting board, a business daily reported Saturday, according to the Kyodo news service. \par \par \uc2  The step is intended to lay the groundwork for concerted market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rapid rise against the dollar, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun said, according to a report picked up by the news service. \par \par \uc2  Kyodo said the report indicates that measures under consideration include substantially expanding the daily fund surplus on the money market from the current 1 trillion yen and providing funds, which can be held by financial institutions until next year, to the market earlier than usual, the paper said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also seeking to diversify the means of funds supply by introducing outright purchases of short-term government securities and increasing the amount of such securities to be bought under resale contracts, the report said. \par \par \uc2  In exchange for concerted action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the U.S. is asking Japan to boost the money supply in addition to taking fiscal stimulus measures through the compilation of a second fiscal 1999 supplementary budget, the paper said, according to Kyodo. \par \par \uc2  At a meeting of the Group of Seven top financial officials in Washington on Sept. 25, Japan will express its readiness to continue stimulating its economy through fiscal and monetary steps, Kyodo quoted the newspaper as saying. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0059GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9i06v0m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
