\par\par \b \uc2  IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  futures trade mixed, yen falls. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 17:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures were mixed early Thursday, as yen pulled back after several days of gains and European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly firmer. December yen fell on speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  would agree to coordinate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Japan to strengthen the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, was in Washington on Thursday to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions with officials from other nations. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan sold yen for dollars last Friday and Tuesday, but its efforts were overwhelmed by strong yen buying led by overseas fund operators, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg indicating interest rates would stay low curbed euro gains, said Mike Malpede, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Inc. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg was quoted in Thursday's Irish Times newspaper as saying the outlook for inflation was favourable and that ECB interest rates would likely remain low into next year. The paper described his comments as his clearest hint yet that rates would remain unchanged at 2.5 percent through 2000. \par \par \uc2  U.S. economic data released early Thursday had little impact on the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  August U.S. industrial output rose 0.3 percent, compared with forecasts for unchanged, and capacity use edged up to 80.8 percent from 80.7 percent in July, compared with forecasts for a dip to 80.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 1035 CDT/1535 GMT, December yen was down $0.000082 at $0.009640, euros up $0.00120 at $1.04800, sterling up $0.0090 at $1.6246, Swiss francs up $0.0011 at $0.6561, Canadian dollars down $0.0006 at $0.6783, Australian dollars down $0.0027 at $0.6473 and Mexican pesos down $0.001150 at $0.102000. \par \par \uc2  ((-Cheryl Jackson, Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750 \par \par \uc2  chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00lkb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
