\par\par \b \uc2  IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  futures close mixed, yen falls. \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 22:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures ended mixed Thursday in light trade tied to shutdowns in New York markets caused by Hurricane Floyd. \par \par \uc2  December yen was down sharply, although well off its overnight low, in selling linked to a weaker Tokyo stock market and some profit-taking, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The contract hovered just above its pit session lows for most of the afternoon as traders speculated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  would agree to coordinate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Japan to strengthen the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, was in Washington Thursday to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions with officials from other nations. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan sold yen for dollars last Friday and Tuesday, but its efforts were overwhelmed by strong yen buying led by overseas fund operators, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "They have to be a little disheartened," said Frank Lesh, vice president and futures analyst at Rand Financial. "Their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't worked. They haven't had anybody else to go in on it with them." \par \par \uc2  Lesh said he thinks U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely, and traders said the yen on Thursday began correcting itself without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I would not call this an end to the trend as of yet," Lesh said. "It's basically been going straight up. It's really due for a little bit of a setback here." \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso also closed sharply lower on jitters tied to the suicide of a former top Mexican prosecutor. Weakness was compounded by thin conditions due to the Independence Day holiday there. \par \par \uc2  The former Mexican deputy attorney general, Mario Ruiz Massieu, faced trial in the United States on money-laundering charges. \par \par \uc2  U.S. economic data released early Thursday had little impact on the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  August U.S. industrial output rose 0.3 percent, compared with forecasts for unchanged, and capacity use edged up to an 80.8 percent rate from 80.7 percent in July, compared with forecasts for a dip to 80.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  At settlement, December yen was down $0.000092 at $0.009630, sterling up $0.0090 at $1.6244, euros up $0.00070 at $1.04750, Swiss francs up $0.0001 at $0.6551, Canadian dollars down $0.0004 at $0.6785, Australian dollars down $0.0032 at $0.6468 and Mexican pesos down $0.000925 at $0.102225. \par \par \uc2  ((-Cheryl Jackson, Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750 \par \par \uc2  chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00i3c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
