\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar plunges to three-yr lows vs. the yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1999\par 18:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 9 (Reuters) - The dollar plummeted to three-year lows against the yen, extending steep overnight declines as yen bulls cheered data showing stronger-than-expected Japanese growth. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell below 108 yen in hectic trade, a decline of more than 3.0 percent from overnight highs above 111 yen. The euro also fell further against the Japanese unit, tumbling below 114 yen to also chalk up declines of more than 3.0 percent from overnight peaks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said earlier that the yen had also received a shot in the arm when William McDonough, president of the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, said the yen is not affecting the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  "Traders took that as a cue to buy more into yen and sell the euro," said Bank of Montreal \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Tom Benfer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's losses may now accelerate very quickly toward the 105 yen level, dealers said, but they added there is some support near the 107.20 yen level. \par \par \uc2  Today's sharp yen gains have put dealers on amber alert for more possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially after senior Japanese officials again warned that any sudden moves would be met with appropriate action. \par \par \uc2  But dealers remained unsure about whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  would participate in any possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly as Washington has remained on the sidelines throughout the summer when the Bank of Japan repeatedly sold dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  ((-N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par