\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-EU recovery may spur  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  action-Wakatsuki. \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 19 (Reuters) - Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become likely if an economic recovery in Germany and the European Union starts to attract more capital to that region, former Bank of Japan (BOJ) Executive Director Mikio Wakatsuki said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think U.S. authorities could maintain their indifference," Wakatsuki told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  The yen hit a seven-month high against the dollar of 111.30 at mid-morning in Tokyo, up nearly two yen from Wednesday. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also struck a lifetime high against the euro of 117.57, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "If the prospects become brighter for Germany and the EU countries, this would attract a flow of capital," Wakatsuki said, "I think the U.S. should not take it too lightly. There is a good chance of joint action." \par \par \uc2  Japan has not sold yen for dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since they last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 21. \par \par \uc2  Wakatsuki said the yen at current levels was not much cause for concern, however, because authorities were ready to act. \par \par \uc2  "It's not a great threat because the situation has changed since last year, and there is greater resistance to a higher yen," Wakatsuki said. \par \par \uc2  He added that the recent strengthening of the yen was "a reflection of a higher Nikkei." \par \par \uc2  When asked whether the BOJ should refrain from sterilising each time it conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Wakatsuki said: "On the point of unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I don't think it's useful at all." \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a more effective way to weaken the yen and indirectly ease credit further. \par \par \uc2  Currently, the BOJ sterilises its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by draining funds from the market after doing so. \par \par \uc2  ((Deborah Collis (813) 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8j024ls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
