\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr dented at close by sluggish asset markets. \b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1999\par 23:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  *Euro/dlr closes higher as U.S. Treasuries tumble more. \par \par \uc2  *Dlr/yen closes unchanged amid ongoing wariness of possible BoJ \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  buoys dollar. Technicians see sell-off to 113.90 \par \par \uc2  possible later this week. Treasury mum on its possible plans. \par \par \uc2  *Dow closes up 31 points, gives dollar a modest lifts. \par \par \uc2  *Sterling, Swiss franc up. Can dlr up on demand for takeover. \par \par \uc2      NEW YORK, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The dollar limped broadly lower \par \par \uc2  in U.S. afternoon trading on Tuesday, bruised by fresh investor \par \par \uc2  sales as the stock market seesawed between gains and losses and \par \par \uc2  the bond market hugged session lows. \par \par \uc2     "Sterling and the euro led the dollar's movement lower; \par \par \uc2  basically it was an investor-driven move," Mellon Bank chief \par \par \uc2  dealer Kevin Lawrie said as thin volumes dried up further. \par \par \uc2     The British pound jumped to $1.6200/10 from $1.6150/60 while \par \par \uc2  euro/dollar bounced to $1.0680/87 from $1.0639/44. The Swiss \par \par \uc2  franc sailed higher too with dollar/Swiss ending at 1.4962/72 \par \par \uc2  from 1.5022/32. \par \par \uc2     Against the yen, the dollar closed unchanged at 115.22/32 \par \par \uc2  yen, having erased modest losses just in time for the close. \par \par \uc2     But the dollar's smallest move of the day still provided the \par \par \uc2  session's biggest talking point -- the chance of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers agreed. \par \par \uc2     Overnight the dollar surged nearly a full yen as Japanese \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa stoked speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 United \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  States\b0 \highlight\uc2  may assist Japan in future \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  when he told \par \par \uc2  parliament that he and U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers \par \par \uc2  had agreed that rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements were unfavourable. \par \par \uc2     Miyazawa however remained mum on any concrete plans and \par \par \uc2  Summers only said he would keep in touch with his colleagues. \par \par \uc2     "The headlines scared us, but then people read the story and \par \par \uc2  realised they weren't saying anything we didn't already know," \par \par \uc2  Paribas chief dealer Dennis Heidt said. \par \par \uc2     Consequently there were some dollar sales but they were \par \par \uc2  modest, dealers said, explaining the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \par \par \uc2  not evaporated even as many said Washington may not assist. \par \par \uc2     "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still in the back of everyone's mind and it \par \par \uc2  is very hard to gauge what the Japanese may do, they have \par \par \uc2  become craftier in their tactics," Lawrie said. \par \par \uc2     If there isn't more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon however, technicians \par \par \uc2  said the dollar could sell off and break below the 114 yen \par \par \uc2  level before the weekend. \par \par \uc2     "The dollar may pause for a day or two and even test higher, \par \par \uc2  but ultimately I think we will be back near 113.60 and lower," \par \par \uc2  Bank of America strategist Ture Johnson said. \par \par \uc2     Meanwhile many dealers also expected the euro to post more \par \par \uc2  gains as Europe's economic landscape brightens and investors \par \par \uc2  appear less enchanted with U.S. assets. Asset markets have been \par \par \uc2  under pressure since last week when higher employment costs \par \par \uc2  sparked talk of a possible rate hike in August. \par \par \uc2  While the benchmark Dow Jones industrial average closed 31 \par \par \uc2  points higher on Tuesday, it had rolled between losses and \par \par \uc2  gains for most of the session leaving some dealers dizzy. \par \par \uc2     Some dealers even began worrying whether the dollar's long \par \par \uc2  reign as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice was coming to an end. \par \par \uc2     "As long as the U.S. was the only game in town ... smart \par \par \uc2  investors were handsomely rewarded for investing in U.S. \par \par \uc2  assets," Larry Hatheway, head of global strategy at Warburg \par \par \uc2  Dillon Read said. \par \par \uc2     But with Europe and Japan showing signs of recovery, the \par \par \uc2  group lowered its 12-month dollar forecasts. \par \par \uc2     In Britain, the construction sector expanded for the sixth \par \par \uc2  straight month in July even though the pace of growth slowed. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said this aided sterling even as dealers were biding \par \par \uc2  their time before the Bank of England's MPC meeting on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday and Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In other trading the dollar lost ground against its northern \par \par \uc2  neighbour, falling to Canadian$1.4918/28 from C$1.4982/92 as a \par \par \uc2  planned takeover was said to have fuelled demand for the \par \par \uc2  Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2     The Australian dollar ended at $0.6543/48, up from \par \par \uc2  $0.6526/36. \par \par \uc2     ((--Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv83037m7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
