\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr erases earlier gains as BOJ fails to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 09:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 21 (Reuters) - The dollar was off earlier highs against the yen by late afternoon on Wednesday in Tokyo as the Bank of Japan (BOJ) had failed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar earlier gained on expectations of another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the Federal Reserve Bank of New York bought dollars for yen overnight on behalf of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Despite the BOJ's absence on Wednesday, caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  still helped discourage dealers from selling dollars aggressively. The dollar was at 118.85/90 yen at 0612 GMT, compared with 118.98/02 yen in New York late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0414/19, steady from $1.0417/20 in late New York, maintaining a firm tone after Germany's Ifo business climate index, released on Tuesday, jumped to a nine-month high in June. \par \par \uc2  "After a surprise Fed move overnight, a lot of people had set up dollar longs, betting that the BOJ would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo today," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo markets were closed on Tuesday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  "But what we got this morning was just verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar dropped as earlier buyers squared longs," the city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa told reporters earlier that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of Japan by the New York Fed overnight demonstrated Japan-U.S. cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa later told a news conference that he thought the yen's sudden rise against the dollar in New York on Tuesday was rapid and should not go unchecked. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Haruhiko Kuroda, vice finance minister for international affairs, reiterated on Wednesday that a premature strengthening of the yen was undesirable before an economic recovery and confirmed that the Fed had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the BOJ's behalf on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But despite the New York Fed's action overnight, dealers were not convinced there was solid accord between Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. \par \par \uc2  "I think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the dollar from going below 115 yen could win international support, as such a drop could jeopardise Japan's economic recovery," said a senior dealer at a Japanese trust bank. \par \par \uc2  "But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around current dollar/yen levels probably will not win strong backing from other countries. As (Economic Planning Agency Minister Taichi) Sakaiya said, a rate of 119 yen (to the dollar) should not pose a grave problem for Japan." \par \par \uc2  Sakaiya said on Wednesday: "Neither a rapid yen rise nor fall is desirable, but the absolute level of the exchange rate is not having a serious impact on the Japanese economy." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the New York Fed on Tuesday began buying dollars from slightly above 118 yen and continued to buy dollars as high as around 119.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly gained against the yen on Wednesday after Standard & Poor's said it had lowered China's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign rating to BBB from BBB-plus, but the news failed to have a lasting impact, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro gained later, with the start of European trade, buoyed by improved sentiment following strong gains on Tuesday in the Ifo German business climate index for June, which jumped to 92.9 from a revised 90.5 in May. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0452/56 at 0651 GMT, reaching its highest level since June 25. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7l044wc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
