\par\par \b \uc2  Japan, US agree on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  action for stability-BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 21 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan (BOJ) Governor Masaru Hayami said on Wednesday neither Japan nor the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  has any major objection to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at stabilising the market. \par \par \uc2  Asked about recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the market view that there were differences between Japan and U.S. policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Hayami told a news conference: "Although I cannot comment on each \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should reflect economic fundamentals, and it is acceptable to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent rapid movements and to stabilise the market. The United States and Japan have no objections (to such action)." \par \par \uc2  Hayami said an increase in overseas investors' purchases of Japanese shares have led to a strengthening in the yen. From January to June, foreigners made net purchases of Japanese stocks totalling a hefty five trillion yen, he said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's term money market interest rates for periods crossing into next year were rising partly due to worries about the millennium computer bug and partly due to expected improvement in the economy, he said. \par \par \uc2  But the rise in such term rates, he added, was not posing any problems for economic conditions or the BOJ's zero interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  He added that the BOJ would continue to watch the impact of millennium bug concerns. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said financial markets were aware that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current zero interest rate policy was extraordinary. \par \par \uc2  Asked about his recent comment that the zero interest rate policy was extraordinary and could not continue forever, which triggered a rise in long-term market interest rates, Hayami said the effect of his remarks disappeared within half a day and he believed the market understood his intent. ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7l03zqn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
