\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr eases vs yen by late Tokyo on exporter selling. \b0\par\par\uc2 695 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 1999\par 09:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 12 (Reuters) - The dollar eased versus yen by late Tokyo on Monday, weighed down by selling by Japanese exporters, but its downside was protected above 122 yen on buying by Japanese and foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan (BOJ) also remained, providing a support. \par \par \uc2  "The topside was capped by exporters' selling," said a city bank dealer. "Their orders are lining up above 123 yen. They're taking into account the chance of (Japan's) future recovery." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 122.00/05 yen at 0625 GMT versus 122.32/42 in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said some Japanese exporters had recently been willing to make forward contracts to hedge chances of a weaker dollar later this year, because Japanese authorities would not stop the dollar's fall against the yen if the Japanese economy picked up in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  There was no verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Since the dollar failed to try the downside last week due to caution over the BOJ's action, it's highly likely to have upward momentum this week," said a trust bank dealer, adding that the rate of 122 yen was firmly protected. \par \par \uc2  Buying by Japanese investors and foreigners' buying to hedge long positions in Tokyo stocks underpinned the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  There was talk of stop-loss dollar sell orders just below 122 yen, but a substantial fall in the dollar was seen as unlikely. \par \par \uc2  "Few people are brave enough to knock the dollar sharply below 122 yen after witnessing the very aggressive BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only a week ago," said another city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 5 to buy dollars, pushing the greenback as high as 122.87 yen on that day from a low of 120.90 yen. Meanwhile, sporadic euro selling against the yen by Japanese investors was detected on Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was 124.18/31 yen at 0700 GMT, against around 124.60 yen in late New York on Friday. Against the dollar, the euro was at $1.0181/83, compared with $1.0179/89 in New York. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were wary about selling the euro too aggressively below 124 yen after rumours on Friday of euro-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ lifted it in overseas markets. The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) to buy the euro against the yen on June 18 and 21. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said a key event for dollar/yen this week may be a scheduled Asia trip by U.S. Treasury Undersecretary for International Affairs Timothy Geithner. \par \par \uc2  Geithner will visit Indonesia, Japan and Taiwan for economic talks from July 13 to 16, a Treasury spokesman said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market will be watching to see if there is any discord between Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following comments by new U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers last week that Tokyo should focus on economic fundamentals rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off remarks by BOJ Policy Board member Eiko Shinotsuka that the overnight rate target should be returned to the average 0.25 percent level it was at before the zero interest rate policy was introduced in February. \par \par \uc2  She made the remarks in a speech to business leaders in Fukui, central Japan. \par \par \uc2  "We all know that Shinotsuka is a hawk. So that was no surprise," said a dealer at another trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Shinotsuka's proposals to tighten the BOJ's ultra-easy monetary policy or at least send a signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can go no further, have been rejected by votes of 8-1 at the board's monetary policy meetings. \par \par \uc2  When asked how soon the BOJ might change monetary policy, Shinotsuka told a news conference later on Monday that she could not speak at all about the timing of a policy change, but said that now was the time for the board to consider her proposals. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7c04s34\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
