\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Japan to wage  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  battle without U.S. help. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1999\par 14:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 5 (Reuters) - Japan's crusade to prevent yen strength from crippling its nascent recovery is expected to be a lonely one given that the United States is contending with a dollar that is near this decade's highs in trade-weighted terms. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges on Monday was the fifth time in less than a month that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold yen. The rhetoric from Japan's finance ministry left little doubt more money would be spent if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Most market analysts agree the impact of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be far greater if the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined in and, crucially, spent money from its own reserves rather than acting as Japan's agent as the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did on June 18. \par \par \uc2  But they saw little chance of such joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the dollar's broad-based strength against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lifted it close to the 1990s trade-weighted high set in August 1998. \par \par \uc2  "It is in the U.S. interests to have a strong dollar but they are very unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dollar/yen," said Ryan Shea, international economist at First Chicago. \par \par \uc2  "They won't want the dollar to get much stronger given their current account deficit is running away towards four percent and this is one of the economic imbalances that the Fed has mentioned." \par \par \uc2  A trade-weighted measure of the dollar's value tracked by the Bank of England closed at 110.3 on Friday, compared with peaks above 115 set in August 1998. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the most recent monthly data released by the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas showed the dollar's trade-weighted index was within two percent of its August 1998 highs by the end of May. \par \par \uc2  Since then the dollar has extended its gains against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rising to eight-year highs against the Swiss franc and rallying to highs against the euro which equate to its best levels this decade against the German mark. "The BOJ could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again but I definitely do not expect Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Stewart Newnham, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at State Street in London. \par \par \uc2  The United States last joined forces with Japan to counteract \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends in June 1998, buying yen on that occasion as the dollar rallied above 140 yen. \par \par \uc2  It last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen in conjunction with Japan in 1995, as part of a concerted effort to lift the dollar decisively away from the post-World War Two lows below 80 yen it had plumbed earlier that year. \par \par \uc2  With the dollar currently at 122 yen, there is little chance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  will mount coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Bank of Japan which involves delving into U.S. reserves, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the dollar is above 100 yen and below 140 yen, it does not appear to be a problem for the U.S.," said Peter von Maydell, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston in London. \par \par \uc2  "They are not in the business of micro-managing exchange rates and if they do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  it will only be as an agent of the BOJ." \par \par \uc2  Against this backdrop, analysts said only signs of a renewed downturn in Japan's economy - the very thing the authorities are trying to prevent - would keep yen bulls at bay. \par \par \uc2  "If all the real economy data shows that Japan is in a self-sustaining recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would become less effective," said Shea at First Chicago. \par \par \uc2  "This is something we do not believe, and if data backs us up, dollar/yen should go higher." \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv75052b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
