\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar falls further on technical sales in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 1998\par 03:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Sept 4 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0029 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar fell further against yen in early Tokyo on Friday, \par \par \uc2  after hitting stop-loss sales at 133.50 yen triggered by \par \par \uc2  remarks by senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. \par \par \uc2      *Top financial diplomat Sakakibara said on Friday that the \par \par \uc2  yen was bound to strengthen further and investors should be \par \par \uc2  aware of such a risk. \par \par \uc2      *Dealers cite more stop-loss sales sitting at 133.00 yen. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar's decline accelerated by sales by Japanese \par \par \uc2  investors to hedge against further dollar falls. \par \par \uc2  *Eisuke Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, also said that Japan was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at an "appropriate" time. \par \par \uc2  *Separately, senior MOF official Haruhiko Kuroda said that the correction of the dollar's excessive strength and the yen's weakness has just begun. He also said there is a possibility that the yen's weakness may be corrected rapidly. \par \par \uc2  *"Although \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears are not so high at these levels, remarks from the senior Finance Ministry officials indicated they are not satisfied with current levels," a dealer at a city bank said." \par \par \uc2  *"Amid continued turmoil in emerging markets, Tokyo dealers are wary of further sales by overseas funds" which has put downward pressure on the dollar, a dealer at a major city bank said. \par \par \uc2  *Institutional investors showed mixed interest in the dollar, dealers said. Some investment trusts were seen selling dollars for hedging purposes, while other investors were picking up dollars near 133.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Meanwhile, Japanese importers and exporters chose to remain on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  *"As there are risks of the dollar falling again, importers are refraining from buying," the second dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *Downside somewhat supported by commercial demand. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers eye U.S. jobs data later on Friday. A weaker-than-expected figure would increase risk on U.S. economy, which is key amid the current emerging markets turmoil, a bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  2302 GMT - *Dollar tumbled below 134 yen in early Asia on Friday on follow-through sales from declines overnight. *Greenback down from sales by overseas fund operators to cover losses incurred in emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar hit low of 133.55 yen, falling below 133.65 yen, the lowest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in mid-June. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar to remain on downward bias on shaky U.S. stocks and continuing turmoil in emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers watching meeting between Japanese Finance Minister Miyazawa and U.S. Treasury Secretary Rubin in San Francisco on Friday. \par \par \uc2  *But they expect the officials to focus on emerging markets' situation, and do not expect any specific action on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy or interest rates. \par \par \uc2  *Rubin said on Thursday: "I think it is absolutely critical, not only for Asia but also for the rest of the world, that Japan gets back on track." Rubin was speaking to reporters on the sidelines of a meeting of U.S., Canadian and Latin American finance officials. \par \par \uc2  *Moody's Investor Services cut foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt rating for Brazil and Venezuela. The rating agency also put Mexico and Argentina on review for possible downgrade. \par \par \uc2  *The dollar closed at 134.05/15 yen and 1.7265/75 marks in New York on Thursday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9400qgu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
