\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar touches three-week low against yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Al Yoon \par \uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 23:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The dollar was lower against the Japanese yen Thursday but slightly above a three-week low it set earlier on lingering speculation that Japan would act to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  President Clinton's announcement that the United States launched military strikes at terrorist bases in Afghanistan and Sudan that were believed to be behind the bombings of two U.S. embassies in Africa this month fuelled light safe-haven dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was steady against the German mark. Concern about the impact of Russia's financial troubles weighed on the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the possibility that the dollar might come under pressure because of the sex scandal in the White House pressured the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped by 2.5 yen in Tokyo, its fall greased after senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda said Japan was willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as low as 141.45 yen before bouncing to 142.97 in late trading, still lower than 144.07 on Wednesday. It was higher at 1.7990 marks from 1.7982. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, reportedly added to his litany of comments warning of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during a visit to the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Aspen, Col. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar rose modestly against the mark following news that suggested Russia's financial crisis may deepen after Moscow's recent rouble devaluation and three-month debt payment moratorium. \par \par \uc2  The dollar firmed after Sergei Aleksashenko, Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first deputy chairman, said that some of Russia's biggest banks could be dragged down by the crisis within a few days, which analysts said puts German lenders at risk. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar-mark is trading sideways, mostly, the equity markets are not looking too healthy and then you've got the Clinton thing in the background," said Robert Fullem, a trader at NatWest Markets. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar was higher at 1.5062 Swiss francs from 1.5060 on Wednesday and the pound rose to $1.6313 from $1.6222. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was lower at Canadian 1.5318 from C$1.5337. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k016jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
