\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr lower at U.S. close, wary of BoJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  *Dlr/mark steadies above support at 1.7825 support, ends lower \par \par \uc2  on early profit-taking, boosted late by Soros statement that FT \par \par \uc2  letter on Russia meant as G7 "wake-up call." *W. House confirms \par \par \uc2  G7 deputies conference call, Rubin talked to Russia. *Dlr/yen \par \par \uc2  holds 145, recovered from brief morning slide. *BoJ jawboning \par \par \uc2  keeps \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat alive. *BoC fails to bolster C$. \par \par \uc2     NEW YORK, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The dollar fell against the \par \par \uc2  yen Thursday as investors remained leery of possible Japanese \par \par \uc2  official yen buying after Japanese officials overnight \par \par \uc2  threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Dollar/mark edged lower on continuing profit-taking that \par \par \uc2  began after a spike higher to 1.80 overnight, though a late \par \par \uc2  session comment on Russia from renowned international financier \par \par \uc2  George Soros gave the greenback a brief boost, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      "Soros seems to be what did it. His comments here and \par \par \uc2  overnight in the Financial Times were driving the market over \par \par \uc2  the course of the day," said a U.S. investment bank dealer. \par \par \uc2      Soros issued a statement saying he hoped major global \par \par \uc2  economic powers would come to Russia's aid as it struggled to \par \par \uc2  overcome a severe cash shortage. \par \par \uc2      He called his letter in Thursday's Financial Times a \par \par \uc2  "wake-up call" for the Group of Seven nations. That letter \par \par \uc2  urged Russia to devalue its battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rouble, and \par \par \uc2  set up a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board. \par \par \uc2      The White House confirmed that finance officials from the \par \par \uc2  G7 on Thursday held a telephone conference call to discuss \par \par \uc2  Russia and that top U.S. financial officials had been in \par \par \uc2  contact with Russian leaders. \par \par \uc2      Ratings agencies Moody's Investors Service and Standard and \par \par \uc2  Poor's Corp. each downgraded Russia on Thursday, though Russia \par \par \uc2  has carried a low-junk status for some time and investors paid \par \par \uc2  little heed to the actions. \par \par \uc2      The dollar ended lower at 1.7845/50 marks from 1.7875/78 at \par \par \uc2  the open. Dollar/yen dipped to 144.95/00 from 145.55/59 at the \par \par \uc2  open and 146.15/25 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2      Concern about yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  heightened overnight after \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, a senior Japanese Finance Ministry official \par \par \uc2  known for his ability to move \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, said Japan was \par \par \uc2  looking for chances to conduct yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers also said the Bank of Japan checked market \par \par \uc2  rates in dollar/yen above 147 overnight, causing investors to \par \par \uc2  dump dollars for fear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might ultimately sell \par \par \uc2  greenbacks for yen. \par \par \uc2      "People now want to take profits at these levels. They must \par \par \uc2  be taking the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat seriously--the dollar doesn't \par \par \uc2  normally go down two big figures when the BoJ checks rates," \par \par \uc2  said Hans Boman, chief spot dealer at Swedbank in New York. \par \par \uc2      The dollar hit an eight-year high at 147.63 yen on Tuesday \par \par \uc2  but has failed to move higher since than as investors have \par \par \uc2  booked profits from a sharp dollar rally in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2      But the dollar's long-term upward trend seemed intact, with \par \par \uc2  dealers stressing no amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could stop the \par \par \uc2  flood of capital to the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and out of battered Asian \par \par \uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      "It's foolish to think that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can have anything \par \par \uc2  but a short-term impact. Given the economic fundamentals, it's \par \par \uc2  not going to turn things around," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Canada again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar, reportedly buying at about C$1.52 to the dollar. But \par \par \uc2  the greenback recovered and continued to move back toward \par \par \uc2  record highs against its Canadian counterpart. \par \par \uc2      "Since last week, the Bank of Canada has used up about $2 \par \par \uc2  billion of reserves and the market has taken that as an \par \par \uc2  opportunity to go out and buy (U.S.) dollars," said Frank \par \par \uc2  Conte, chief dealer at Royal Bank of Canada in New York." \par \par \uc2     "There is still a shortage of U.S. dollars there, and the \par \par \uc2  market is saying 'thanks very much.'" \par \par \uc2      The dollar rose to Canadian $1.5198/03 from C$1.5155/60 at \par \par \uc2  the open and edged higher to 1.4890/00 Swiss francs from \par \par \uc2  1.4888/98. Sterling dipped to $1.6240/45 from $1.6242/52. The \par \par \uc2  Australian dollar rose to $0.