\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - Yen seen stalling before heading even lower vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Pratima Desai \par \uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (In London item MARKETS-YEN please read in fourth paragraph '...six-week highs...' correcting figure. A corrected repetition follows.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 31 (Reuters) - Japan's besieged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to take a breather after its slide to six-week lows against the dollar on Friday but will head lower again in the coming week, analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The major focus on the downside is now on 146.75 per dollar, the near eight-year high seen in the middle of June, just before the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen's latest downmove showed the market's disappointment at the new government's failure to take the initiative at the earliest opportunity to reform the recession-hit economy. It also reflected the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the yen is unlikely at this stage. \par \par \uc2  The catalyst for dollar/yen's surge to new six-week (corrects) highs was the comments by Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa after he took up his new post at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said he believed in leaving the yen and stock prices to the markets, except in exceptional circumstances such as the Japan-U.S. joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mid-June. \par \par \uc2  "Next week dollar/yen will target 146.75," said Audrey-Childe Freeman, European economist at CIBC in London. "We may see another surge in the dollar after the U.S. open, but 145.00 yen is an important psychological level." \par \par \uc2  In the European morning, a heavily bid dollar rose to 144.50 yen and slipped back only marginally to 144.36/46 by 1105 GMT, up from 142.33/43 in late European trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Side-by-side with the dollar, the mark rose against the yen. The mark was last at 81.05/08 yen, near 81.11, the highest since October 1992 and up from 80.53/56 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Jane Foley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital also sees the dollar testing 146.75 yen next week. \par \par \uc2  "Miyazawa's comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an extreme situation clarified his position. It has distanced market fears of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The yen has probably not seen its weakest point yet. On a 12-month view, Barclays Capital see dollar/yen at 175.00 and mark/yen at 89.70. \par \par \uc2  Economic data on the economy released overnight added fuel to the yen bears' attack. \par \par \uc2  Unemployment rose to a record 4.3 percent in June from 4.1 in May, while nationwide consumer prices were up just 0.1 percent year-on-year in June after a rise of 0.5 percent in May. \par \par \uc2  "The data points to a depressionary economic situation," said Childe-Freeman." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said vital fiscal reforms to boost consumer confidence and consumption are necessary but financial sector reforms are more important in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  "Japan has said they want to be aggressive on fiscal reforms, but without reform in the banking sector a sustainable economic recovery will be difficult," Childe-Freeman said, echoing U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin. \par \par \uc2  Rubin said Thursday the "single most important thing" was for Japan to implement effective bank reform quickly. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said it was important that banking problems be fixed fast and domestic demand stimulated promptly. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it is not appropriate and does \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it is appropriate. \par \par \uc2  Childe-Freeman said Summer's comments had also contributed to reducing fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The New York Federal Reserve reported on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total of $833 million on June 17, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since August 1995. \par \par \uc2  A proposal by Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party aimed at providing liquidity for sound borrowers of failed financial institutions was originally applauded by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "But the time-lags on all the proposals to do with fiscal and financial reform are disappointing and will continue to weigh on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Foley said. "I think there is more disappointment to come through on the pace of reform." \par \par \uc2  As \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets become more impatient, long dollar and mark positions against the yen will grow, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "But that only sets us up for a huge bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen," a trader cautioned. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du7v01882\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
