\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar steady, well-supported in early Tokyo trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 02:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, July 31 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0003 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar steady against yen in early Tokyo trade, retaining \par \par \uc2  solid tone after concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  receded on overnight comments by new Finance Minister Kiichi \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2      *Miyazawa told news conference early on Friday he basically \par \par \uc2  believes in leaving yen and stock prices to markets. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar supported by month-end commercial demand and buying \par \par \uc2  related to setting up of fresh trust funds. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar/yen at 143.65/68, versus 143.68/73 in New York. \par \par \uc2  *Profit-taking and Japanese exporter offers likely to slow pace of dollar rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *"Exporters are likely to see 143 yen as good level to sell dollars before the holiday break (in mid-August)," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *But dealers said dollar could receive boost if Japan's jobs data, due out around 0030 GMT, shows further deterioration in jobs conditions. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said market would be watching for any comments from finance ministry officials that might clarify overnight comments by Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  *Miyazawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was appropriate in "extreme cases", such as recent Japan-U.S. joint yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *"People want to see if there is going to be a shift in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  *There was little reaction to comments by Deputy U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers that \b \highlight22\uc2 United States intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it is appropriate and does not when it is not. \par \par \uc2  *Summers told CNN Japan needed to act promptly to resolve problems in its banking sector and stimulate domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  *The New York Federal Reserve reported on Thursday that U.S. sold a total of $833 million on June 17, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for first time since August 1995. New York Fed declined to comment on volume of dollar sales by Japan during that joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *Dollar moved narrowly near 1.7800 marks in early Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers expected dollar/mark to remain trapped in tight range ahead of release of second-quarter U.S. gross domestic product data at 1230 GMT Friday. \par \par \uc2  *"I don't think dollar/mark will move very far from 1.78 before the U.S. GDP data," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  2300 GMT - \par \par \uc2  *Dollar steady versus yen in early Asia, seen likely to maintain strong tone after being boosted overnight by comments from new Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  *"I think selling by Japanese exporters and profit-taking will emerge and push the dollar/yen lower in early trade. But the dollar will probably not fall back below 143 yen today," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *If Japanese jobs data for June, due out Friday morning, shows further deterioration in conditions, yen could come under more pressure, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *In addition to Japanese data, market will be nervously watching whether finance ministry officials will make comments to clarify Miyazawa's overnight remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *"To say that Miyazawa's comments last night mean a major change in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy may be a bit premature. We will have to see," said a dealer at another city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Mark expected to continue to attract buying interest from Japanese investors, but Japanese exporter sales could slow its rise, dealers said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du7v00oei\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
