\par\par \b \uc2  OPTIONS - Dollar/yen vols buoyed as spot slides. \b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1998\par 21:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, June 30 (Reuters) - Dollar/yen implied volatilities perked up Tuesday as the spot retreated, slipping briefly to 138 yen in U.S. trade from overnight highs above 142 yen. \par \par \uc2  Fear that another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could accompany a draft of Japan's bridge bank plan due out Thursday pressured the dollar versus the yen and pushed the one-month dollar/yen risk reversal to a strong yen call skew, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The risk reversal, or put-call pricing differential, on standard one-month options ended at 0.6/0.8 for yen calls, out from 0.45/0.7 in the morning and a slim yen call bias Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen volatilities jumped to 17.85/18.1 percent for one-month dates from 17.0/17.3 percent the day before, and soared to 16.9/17.15 percent in one-year from 15.7/15.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  Volatilities were already swollen, as spot has careened from 146.75 yen before the June 17 U.S.-Japan joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a low of 133.60 and back up again. The dollar stood at 139.00 yen late in the U.S. afternoon. \par \par \uc2  They veered higher again Tuesday in response to the spot's fall after the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was revived, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Spot moves bear out the fact that dollar/yen continues to remain very volatile," said Soma Rao, first vice president for Salomon Smith Barney. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, speaking in Bangkok Tuesday, called the joint U.S.-Japan dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  two weeks ago "very constructive" and indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Also, former \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Tomomitsu Oba overnight said concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible after details on Japan's bridge bank plan are announced Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Rao said dollar/yen volatilities could remain inflated despite the upcoming three-day U.S. Independence Day holiday weekend given an unwillingness to sell options in the current uncertain environment. "People are finding it difficult to be short options," Rao said. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/mark volatility was steady at 8.0/8.3 percent with spot hovering just under 1.81 marks, off Monday's peaks, overshadowed by activity in the yen. \par \par \uc2  U.S. bank dealers said interest in South African rand puts picked up before the country releases reserves data Thursday. One-month dollar/rand volatility was quoted at 25/32 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Susan Kelly, Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750 chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6u01x7k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
