\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr ends quiet US mixed before FOMC, payrolls. \b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1998\par 23:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  *Quiet dlr/mark firmer. Russia woes pressure mark, RTS -6.11 \par \par \uc2  pct. Mkt eyes 2-day FOMC start Tues, June US payrolls Thurs. \par \par \uc2   *Russia seeks faster $500-$600 mln World Bank payout due Oct. \par \par \uc2   *Rangy dlr/yen off. Poor Japan econ outlook props, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  fears cap. Yen sales abate as LDP bridge bank details awaited \par \par \uc2  Thurs. *Strong Dow seen dlr lure on flight from emerging mkts. \par \par \uc2     NEW YORK, June 29 (Reuters) - The dollar ended mixed in \par \par \uc2  quiet trade, with the mark losing support amid speculation that \par \par \uc2  Germany's large investments in Russia were being jeopardised by \par \par \uc2  Moscow's mounting financial crisis, traders said. \par \par \uc2      Activity was extremely light ahead of a two-day meeting of \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve policy makers on Tuesday and Wednesday, the \par \par \uc2  widely watched monthly U.S. employment report on Thursday and \par \par \uc2  the Fourth of July long weekend starting Friday. \par \par \uc2      "The market is just digesting everything. It's going to get \par \par \uc2  ready to have a big move in the next couple of days," said \par \par \uc2  Russell LaScala, chief dealer at Citibank. \par \par \uc2      The dollar slipped to 141.65/75 yen, from 141.73/83 at the \par \par \uc2  open. It rose to 1.8105/15 marks from 1.8080/90. \par \par \uc2      The mark weakened against the yen and pound after the World \par \par \uc2  Bank said the Russian government had asked it to speed up \par \par \uc2  payment of a $500-to-$600 million loan due in October, to help \par \par \uc2  Moscow make up worrisome budget shortfalls. \par \par \uc2  Investor confidence in Russia's ability to cover its \par \par \uc2  deficits, and retain enough \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to avert a \par \par \uc2  devaluation of the rouble, has been evaporating rapidly in \par \par \uc2  recent days. \par \par \uc2  Fears about Russia's ability to meet debt payments \par \par \uc2  resurfaced last week, even though the International Monetary \par \par \uc2  Fund okayed the release of a delayed $670 million payment. \par \par \uc2      Germany, one of Russia's largest lenders, is seen most at \par \par \uc2  risk if the country defaults on its international obligations. \par \par \uc2      The market is looking for the IMF to grant $10-$15 billion \par \par \uc2  in new emergency loans. But the agency is only willing to let \par \par \uc2  go of that money if Russia undertakes real economic reform. \par \par \uc2      Russia's benchmark RTS share index closed down 6.11 percent \par \par \uc2  and yields on Russian Treasury securities rose again on Monday, \par \par \uc2  after soaring to around 70 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2      The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps pushing up interest rates, \par \par \uc2  finding it increasingly difficult to attract the foreign \par \par \uc2  capital it needs to cover its short-term cash flow needs. \par \par \uc2      Overnight, the dollar rose to 143.35 yen, its highest level \par \par \uc2  since Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets nearly two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2      The dollar erased those early gains after the Bank of Japan \par \par \uc2  released its quarterly tankan report of business confidence, \par \par \uc2  which showed that sentiment, while gloomy, was better than \par \par \uc2  expected. The diffusion index came in at minus 38, versus \par \par \uc2  forecasts of -42 or worse and the March tankan, which was -31. \par \par \uc2  Yen trading was focused on Thursday's expected release of \par \par \uc2  the outline of Japan's bridge bank plan to take over the assets \par \par \uc2  of failed financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen remained in a tight range. Lingering fears of \par \par \uc2  more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  discouraged buying, but the dollar was mostly \par \par \uc2  supported above 141.50 by ongoing alarm about Japan's \par \par \uc2  distressed economy. \par \par \uc2  "The strength of the dollar against the yen is also helping \par \par \uc2  to hold up the dollar-mark," said a trader at a German bank. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. stocks have been going really strong the last week and \par \par \uc2  that's helping it as well." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the pound slipped a hair to $1.6660/70 from \par \par \uc2  $1.6665/75 at the open. The dollar inched up to 1.5225/35 Swiss \par \par \uc2  from 1.5220/30 and to Canadian $1.4702/07 from C$1.4698/03. \par \par \uc2      The Australian dollar closed at $0.6070/75, up from \par \par \uc2  $0.6055/65. \par \par \uc2      ((--Alden Bentley, 212 859 1667)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6t01uf4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
