\par\par \b \uc2  US monitors timing of possible  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -Rubin. \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, June 26 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to monitor closely the timing of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said that sometimes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was appropriate, and sometimes it was not. Rubin, on a visit to China as part of a tour by President Bill Clinton, repeated that the key to the yen's stability was Japan taking action on its economy. \par \par \uc2  He said China and the whole world were very focused on the Japanese economic situation. \par \par \uc2  Rubin was speaking to reporters after meeting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong, Finance Minister Xiang Huaicheng and Prime Minister Zhu Rongji. \par \par \uc2  "They are very focused on the economic situation in Japan," Rubin said. He said concern was expressed about the adverse impact of the weak yen on the region. \par \par \uc2  "The key to all this is what Japan does," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The whole world is focused on the need for Japan to take action," he said. \par \par \uc2  "While the key is that Japan takes effective action with respect to their economy and particularly their banking system, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can also be appropriate under some circumstances," Rubin said. \par \par \uc2  "It will not be appropriate under other circumstances," he added. \par \par \uc2  "It is something we watch very closely on a regular basis," he said. \par \par \uc2  "There's a great deal of focus in Asia to get back on track ... there was a recognition that this is a process that is going to take time," Rubin said. \par \par \uc2  "The concern in all these meetings was the economic conditons in Japan," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar at one point on Friday rose to its highest level against the yen since June 17 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the plummeting Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar/yen was trading around 141.80 at 1200 GMT after hitting a nine-day high of 142.98. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q020we\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
