\par\par \b \uc2  IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  futures close pit trade mostly lower. \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 21:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, June 26 (Reuters) - IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures cut losses late but still ended pit trading mostly lower. \par \par \uc2  Into the close, the futures arm of a French-owned bank bought 800 September yen and hit some buystops, brokers said. The same firm purchased roughly 500 September Swiss francs, which had slumped to a new contract low near midday. \par \par \uc2  But the late uptick proved fleeting, and September Swiss sagged again when the firm stopped buying, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  They called the Swiss unit's drop largely technical in nature after it had punched below key support outright and in crosses. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's been technical for 66, 70 (points) down," said a floor broker of September Swiss' drop to a low at $0.6580. "It's (performance) so poor. It didn't bounce, didn't bounce. I think it's overdone, but you can't step into it." \par \par \uc2  Before midday, lead-month September \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board sagged to the day's low as jitters about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly took a back seat to pre-weekend position adjustment, technicals and signs of safety-seeking flows into the dollar as Russia tightened credit to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday raised its refinancing rate to 80 percent from 60 percent, from Monday. \par \par \uc2  Russia's prime minister shortly thereafter said the Russian government had never discussed devaluing the rouble. \par \par \uc2  The market also fretted about whether central banks might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sunday night when Japan releases its quarterly Tankan survey of business sentiment that is expected to show continued weakness and possibly batter the yen again. \par \par \uc2  Unconfirmed reports the Federal Reserve and other central banks may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday to shore up the South African rand appeared to limit losses in most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some pundits figured the rand \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  simply reminded the market that central banks would stay on alert. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury secretary Robert Rubin said early on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to closely monitor the timing of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that the key to yen stability is for Japan to take effective action and that sometimes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is appropriate and sometimes not. \par \par \uc2  May's U.S. personal income rose 0.5 percent and spending increased 0.6 percent, exactly as-expected. \par \par \uc2  Sept yen rose $0.000013 to $0.007119, marks lost $0.0030 to $0.5552, Swiss fell $0.0030 to $0.6605, sterling fell $0.0088 to $1.6554, Can dlr up $0.0002 to $0.6832, Aussie flat at $0.6048, and Mexican peso fell $0.000825 to $0.106400. \par \par \uc2  ((Chicago Derivatives Desk(312)408-8750 chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q01zom\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
