\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/mark ends US up, buoyed by Russia crisis. \b0\par\par\uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 23:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  *Dlr/mark up on safe-haven buys as Russia woes linger after \par \par \uc2  Moscow \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hikes rates to 80 pct from 60 pct to defend \par \par \uc2  rouble. Break of 1.8150 could signal retest of key 1.85 level. \par \par \uc2   *Dlr/yen modestly higher but off session highs amid fears of \par \par \uc2  new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Rubin's comments in China. \par \par \uc2   *Mkt fears \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as soon as late Sunday, early Monday. \par \par \uc2      NEW YORK, June 26 (Reuters) - The dollar ended a busy week \par \par \uc2  higher against the mark and the yen on Friday as concerns about \par \par \uc2  Russia's and Japan's financial crises prompted investors to \par \par \uc2  seek safety in U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2      Dollar/mark ended at 1.8095/05, a full pfennig above its \par \par \uc2  1.7994/97 opening level while dollar/yen stood at 141.85/95, \par \par \uc2  modestly above the 141.73/83 open. \par \par \uc2      Dealers however noted that closing prices failed to \par \par \uc2  accurately reflect the day's events where one crisis after the \par \par \uc2  next seemed to spawn an endless succession of rumours, leading \par \par \uc2  to very nervous trading conditions. \par \par \uc2      "It was a totally crazy day and I am dead," lamented John \par \par \uc2  Schein, vice president at Generale Bank. \par \par \uc2      News that Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by 20 \par \par \uc2  percentage points to 80 percent, effective Monday, cast a \par \par \uc2  shadow over the mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Moscow's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the step only one day after the \par \par \uc2  International Monetary Fund agreed to unblock a stalled $670 \par \par \uc2  million in aid to Russia. Still, the rouble still fell outside \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bands and domestic debt prices plummeted as \par \par \uc2  dealers reported new fears that reforms may be stalled. \par \par \uc2      "The Russian situation has weighed on the mark," said Marc \par \par \uc2  Chandler, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank Securities. \par \par \uc2      But dealers said it was not the only reason investors were \par \par \uc2  exiting the mark, noting that the dollar was simply being seen \par \par \uc2  as the safest investment at the moment. \par \par \uc2      "I am still very bullish for dollar/mark and a break of \par \par \uc2  1.8160 could signal another test of the year's highs around \par \par \uc2  1.8562," Chandler added. \par \par \uc2      Even as dollar/mark posted the day's larger gains, dealers \par \par \uc2  had not lost sight of dollar/yen, still expressing intense \par \par \uc2  interest in buying dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2      "I still think the bet is to buy more dollar/yen," another \par \par \uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2      Investors expressed new disappointment with Japan's lack of \par \par \uc2  reform efforts even as talk of a possible bank merger seemed to \par \par \uc2  suggest new steps were being taken to overhaul the nation's \par \par \uc2  frail banking system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd. and Sumitomo Trust & \par \par \uc2  Banking Co., Ltd. are mulling a possible merger. \par \par \uc2      "Japan remains the same, there is no trust policymakers are \par \par \uc2  cleaning house. There is a lot of talk of reform but last \par \par \uc2  week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was only a Band-Aid," Schein said. \par \par \uc2      At the same time however, investors were frightened off from \par \par \uc2  more aggressive dollar buying after Treasury Secretary Robert \par \par \uc2  Rubin, travelling in China with U.S. President Bill Clinton, \par \par \uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to closely monitor the timing \par \par \uc2  for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week joined Japan and spent billions \par \par \uc2  of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stabilise the yen, buying \par \par \uc2  yen for the first time in six years. Although the yen climbed \par \par \uc2  six percent last week, gains have nearly evaporated this week. \par \par \uc2      The Federal Reserve Bank of New York was also seen selling \par \par \uc2  dollars for South African rand on Friday, acting as an agent. \par \par \uc2      Neither the Fed nor the Reserve Bank commented on the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which appeared fruitless as the rand stabilised \par \par \uc2  only briefly before plummeting to a new record low at 5.9605 to \par \par \uc2  the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In other trading the British pound slipped to $1.6610/20 \par \par \uc2  from $1.6655/65 and the dollar climbed against the Swiss franc \par \par \uc2  to 1.5265/75 from 1.5159/64. The dollar also edged higher \par \par \uc2  against the Canadian dollar to C$1.4693/98 from C$1.4650/55. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar ended at $0.6018/25 down from its \par \par \uc2  $0.6062/67 open. \par \par \uc2  ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q01ylj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
