\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar mixed as Russia crisis helps, Rubin comments hurt. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 23:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 26 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against the German mark on Friday on fears Russia's financial crisis may worsen, but it slipped against the Japanese yen amid worries central banks may soon attempt to stabilise the yen further. \par \par \uc2  Only one day after the International Monetary Fund agreed to unblock a stalled $670 million in aid to Russia, the ruble fell outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bands and domestic debt prices plummeted on fears that reforms may be stalled. \par \par \uc2  Determined to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its key refinancing rate by 20 percentage points to 80 percent, effective on Monday. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders remained worried nonetheless and shifted funds into dollars, often considered a safer investment than the mark because of Germany's close ties with Russia. \par \par \uc2  "The Russian situation has weighed on the mark," said Marc Chandler, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon trading, the dollar stood at 1.8090 marks, over a full pfennig above Thursday's 1.7980 close. Against the yen, the dollar was at 141.98, fractionally below Thursday's 142.07 close, and off the 142.90 high seen earlier in the New York day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had managed to reach that high as investors expressed new disappointment with Japan's lack of reform efforts even as talk of a possible bank merger seemed to suggest new steps were being taken to overhaul the nation's frail banking system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan and Sumitomo Trust & Banking Co., Ltd. were reported to be mulling a merger. \par \par \uc2  "The situation in Japan remains the same, there is no trust that policy-makers are cleaning house. There is a lot of talk of reform but last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop the yen was merely a Band-Aid," said John Schein, vice president at Generale Bank. \par \par \uc2  At the same time however, investors were frightened off more aggressive dollar buying after Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, travelling in China with President Bill Clinton, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to closely monitor the timing for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week joined Japan in spending billions of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stabilise the yen, buying yen for the first time in six years. Although the yen climbed 6 percent last week, gains have nearly evaporated this week. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve Bank of New York was also said to have sold dollars for South African rand on Friday, acting as an agent for the Reserve Bank of South Africa, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Neither the Fed nor the Reserve Bank commented on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which appeared fruitless as the rand stabilised only briefly before plummeting to a new record low at $5.9605 to the rand. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the British pound slipped to $1.6615 from $1.6717 and the dollar climbed against the Swiss franc to 1.5263 from 1.5160. The dollar also edged higher against the Canadian dollar to C$1.4688 from C$1.4662. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q01yjg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscale