\par\par \b \uc2  At key pivot, dollar/yen bulls ponder  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Al Yoon \par \uc2 627 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1998\par 18:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 25 (Reuters) - Dollar/yen bulls were chomping at the bit on Thursday but key technical levels and memories of last week's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave reason to pause in U.S. trading, market-watchers said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback on Thursday briefly powered past 142 yen, approaching the level where U.S. and Japanese officials began selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  That surge eclipsed one key technical flashpoint and left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the verge of a fresh break to recent highs, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Technicals, and the fundamental fact that that's where the Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week" put a lid on dollar/yen early, said Jeremy Fand, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BankBoston, who added some dealers expected a rough 135-140 range to persist. \par \par \uc2  Any convincing move past 142 yen could herald a quick dollar pop higher, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said 141.70/80 represented a 61.8-percent Fibonacci retracement of dollar/yen's fall from its recent eight-year high of 146.75 to the post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  low of 133.60. \par \par \uc2  Further, 141.67 was the high of June 10, an important pivot just before the more dramatic move toward 146. But the break beyond that area could nullify resistances, said John Tirone, technical analyst at Chase Securities. \par \par \uc2  "This is the level that we broke out to and the next day we saw 144.40. So psychologically it could have the same effect if we have a strong move in this area," Tirone said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen hovered close to 141.50 for much of the morning in New York. Some traders reported accounts holding the rally back with fresh short-dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market action earlier on Thursday reflected sharper, albeit shallow, downmoves compared to upmoves, which signalled an indecisive market. In the end, there may not be a compelling reason to test \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resolve, they added. \par \par \uc2  "People have to take \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seriously ... anytime the dollar goes from 142 yen to 133 in a very short period of time, it could be very costly to be doubtful," said Tom Arnold, chief dealer at Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  Still, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears at the top, Arnold stressed that a lot of accounts had a "real need to buy dollars on the downside." \par \par \uc2  Fand said the market was focused on news-driven risks rather than the negative economic fundamentals that have pushed the yen sharply lower for the past year. \par \par \uc2  With parliamentary elections in Japan looming next month, dealers doubted Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto's Liberal Democratic Party would offer any policy proposals that might shake the market soon, he said. \par \par \uc2  "People want answers and will wait for something on the political side with (U.S. President Bill) Clinton in China or on the bank loan issue out of Japan," said Fand, who added that many accounts were unwilling to take speculative positions after the losses they've seen in the past week. \par \par \uc2  Clinton began a nine-day trip to China on Thursday. Dealers were watchful for talk of yuan stability after some speculation last week that Chinese pressure helped convince the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to join Japan in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Fand was dubious that another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was near, with U.S. officials seen more worried about the pace of the yen's fall than actual levels. Last week's move with Japan was a one-off event buying time for the Japanese to craft a policy response that could anchor the yen for now, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dai-Ichi Kangyo's Arnold said the yen would likely continue to weaken, fuelling speculation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations. \par \par \uc2  ((-N.A. Treasury desk, 212-859-1672)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6p024rv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
