\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-China says hopes for more US-Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mure Dickie \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 1998\par 14:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 20 (Reuters) - Chinese financial officials on Saturday basked in international praise for their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, praised recent U.S. action to support the yen and called on Japan to make real efforts to boost its economy. \par \par \uc2  At a hastily called regional meeting in Tokyo to discuss Asia's economic crisis, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice Governor Liu Mingkang said China hoped for more of the same after Washington and Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the yen. \par \par \uc2  "We really welcome the U.S.-Japan joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was successful," Liu said in a telephone interview. \par \par \uc2  "We also hope they will continue this kind of action," Liu said. \par \par \uc2  In a surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, the Bank of Japan and the New York Federal Reserve sold billions of dollars for yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets - a move that followed repeated calls from Beijing for action to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  China says that selfless efforts to maintain the value of its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as other regional units plummet were made even more painful by the yen's slide to near an eight-year low in the days before the joint Japan-U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said Johnson Smick International Inc, a Washington consulting group, had reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the yen after Chinese officials told them they could no longer hold off devaluing the yuan - which has been widely seen as an island of exchange stability in Asia's economic storm. \par \par \uc2  In an interview released on Saturday, U.S. President Bill Clinton said he would take the opportunity of a China visit that starts next week to urge Beijing not to devalue the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Chinese officials were gratified by a statement issued after the meeting of senior officials from Asian countries and the Group of Seven industrial nations that welcomed China's oft-stated commitment to maintain yuan stability. \par \par \uc2  "We are very pleased that the deputies took note of the contributions made by China to help restore confidence in this region," said Chinese Assistant Minister of Finance Jin Liqun. \par \par \uc2  "The Chinese government is firm on its commitment to maintain the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Jin told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The meeting, called at short notice and held amid journalist packs and bewildered foreign tourists at a Tokyo hotel, also gave Chinese officials a chance to sit down in private with U.S. counterparts ahead of Clinton's landmark five-city tour. \par \par \uc2  Liu and Jin met U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers over room-service coffees on the 37th floor of the gathering's downtown hotel venue. \par \par \uc2  "We had a good discussion," Summers said as he left the bilateral meeting. Both sides declined to elaborate. \par \par \uc2  While Liu and Jin praised the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts of the United States, they spiced a welcome for Tokyo's vows of determined action to restructure the Japanese financial system with calls for action to be carried out quickly and visibly. \par \par \uc2  Japan says it is determined to restructure its financial system by disposing of bad loans burdening the financial sector, accelerating economy-boosting steps and reforming its tax system. \par \par \uc2  China joined in welcoming such plans - but Tokyo should move quickly, Jin said. \par \par \uc2  "We think it is very important for the Japanese government to implement all these policy announcements very promptly," he said. ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 3744 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6k02btx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
