\par\par \b \uc2  Yen starts European trading firm near 3-wk high. \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 09:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 18 (Reuters) - The Japanese yen started European trading on Thursday firm but off a three-week high set in the Asian session after the central banks of the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Federal Reserve and Bank of Japan to sell dollars for yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market sparked a rally which catapulted the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 135.50 against the dollar in overnight Asian trading, its strongest in three weeks. \par \par \uc2  By 0715 GMT the yen had slipped back to 137.02 per dollar, holding on to the bulk of the six-percent gain it had made on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had subsided, the market remained nervous on Thursday and traders were watching for any news emerging from U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers' visit to Tokyo. Summers is due to meet Japan's Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga and other senior officials. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were also alert ahead of the meeting of deputy finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the Group of Seven nations which will also be held in Tokyo this weekend. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yen fell to its weakest in nearly eight years at 146.75 per dollar. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been weakening against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for many months due to a stream of depressing news about the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  The yen was also on a firm footing against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday in line with its gains against the dollar. It rose to a four-week high against the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 76.15 per mark, and a two-week peak against sterling at 226.60 per pound. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom, +44 171-542-6721, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .newszreuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02rin\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (United States near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995